<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JCI buys all Shell S.Africa coal interests.</title>
<headline>JCI buys all Shell S.Africa coal interests.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>JCI Ltd said on Wednesday that Ingwe Coal Corp Ltd had declined to exercise its pre-emptive rights to 50 percent of Shell South Africa's Rietspruit Joint Venture.</p>
<p>As a result, JCI had acquired the whole of Shell's coal business in South Africa, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>In April, JCI said it's wholly-owned subsidiary Tavistock Colliery Ltd had acquired Shell South Africa's -- a unit of Royal Dutch Shell -- coal business for 440 million rand.</p>
<p>&quot;Rietspruit has always been a reliable supplier in the coal business and will complement Tavistock's export drive,&quot; Tavistock chief executive John Dreyer said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
